{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JqkJQdLtTYeyC6mC5SpBAY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Intervals.icu OAuth API scopes ACTIVITY:READ WELLNESS:READ CALENDAR authorize token refresh_token expires_in\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu OAuth support\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\"},{\"title\":\"# Überauth intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://repo.hex.pm/preview/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.2/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Überauth intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0\"},{\"title\":\"OAuth support\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759/14\"},{\"title\":\"docs.treedis.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.treedis.com/reference/models/OAuth2TokenData\"},{\"title\":\"Obtain a new access token\",\"url\":\"https://docs.talkdesk.com/reference/authentication-1\"},{\"title\":\"Obtain a new access token\",\"url\":\"https://docs.talkdesk.com/reference/oauth-token-post\"},{\"title\":\"www.papermark.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.papermark.com/docs/api/scopes\"},{\"title\":\"systemedx.com\",\"url\":\"https://systemedx.com/API/AuthorizationTechnical.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up useful detail on Intervals.icu's OAuth flow, but the official forum post was cut off before the token response, so I could not confirm the `expires_in` or `refresh_token` fields from an official source.\n\n- **Authorization and token exchange:** Intervals.icu's forum post on its OAuth support describes sending users to its authorize URL with `client_id`, `redirect_uri`, `scope`, and `state`. The app then has to exchange the returned code at its token endpoint within 2 minutes, using `client_id` and `client_secret`. If all goes well Intervals.icu will respond with an access token, granted scopes and the id and name of the athlete.\n- **Scope format:** A third-party Elixir library README says intervals.icu joins scopes with commas, not the spaces used by most OAuth 2.0 providers. The same source lists ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, and CALENDAR, each with a :READ or :WRITE suffix, and says the default is ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ.\n- **Tokens and refresh:** The same library README states that there is no refresh token and no expiry. This comes from a non-official source, so it should be checked against Intervals.icu's own API docs before you rely on it.\n- **Other limits:** A forum reply says there can be many access tokens for an athlete linked to an app, once for each time they authorise it. It also says OAuth tokens grant access to the authorising athlete's data but not to people they follow or coach. The library README adds that the ATHLETES scope does not work with bearer tokens, where it returns 403.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36b9e331-29f4-4cd2-ab10-f29d34554d46","uuid":"3407271b-c00c-417e-b6c9-44896c06838b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:54:56.567Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Intervals.icu OAuth API scopes ACTIVITY:READ WELLNESS:READ CALENDAR authorize token refresh_token expires_in","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XiLCW5hDeSvtwG15YhxCeY","content":[{"title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759"},{"title":"# Überauth intervals.icu","url":"https://repo.hex.pm/preview/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.2/README.md"},{"title":"Überauth intervals.icu","url":"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0"},{"title":"OAuth support","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759/14"},{"title":"docs.treedis.com","url":"https://docs.treedis.com/reference/models/OAuth2TokenData"},{"title":"Obtain a new access token","url":"https://docs.talkdesk.com/reference/authentication-1"},{"title":"Obtain a new access token","url":"https://docs.talkdesk.com/reference/oauth-token-post"},{"title":"www.papermark.com","url":"https://www.papermark.com/docs/api/scopes"},{"title":"systemedx.com","url":"https://systemedx.com/API/AuthorizationTechnical.html"}]},"The search turned up useful detail on Intervals.icu's OAuth flow, but the official forum post was cut off before the token response, so I could not confirm the `expires_in` or `refresh_token` fields from an official source.\n\n- **Authorization and token exchange:** Intervals.icu's forum post on its OAuth support describes sending users to its authorize URL with `client_id`, `redirect_uri`, `scope`, and `state`. The app then has to exchange the returned code at its token endpoint within 2 minutes, using `client_id` and `client_secret`. If all goes well Intervals.icu will respond with an access token, granted scopes and the id and name of the athlete.\n- **Scope format:** A third-party Elixir library README says intervals.icu joins scopes with commas, not the spaces used by most OAuth 2.0 providers. The same source lists ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, and CALENDAR, each with a :READ or :WRITE suffix, and says the default is ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ.\n- **Tokens and refresh:** The same library README states that there is no refresh token and no expiry. This comes from a non-official source, so it should be checked against Intervals.icu's own API docs before you rely on it.\n- **Other limits:** A forum reply says there can be many access tokens for an athlete linked to an app, once for each time they authorise it. It also says OAuth tokens grant access to the authorising athlete's data but not to people they follow or coach. The library README adds that the ATHLETES scope does not work with bearer tokens, where it returns 403."],"durationSeconds":6.272105958999997,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JqkJQdLtTYeyC6mC5SpBAY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
