{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzFtdWP4grMWMv5ihbS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U4Ewg9ydTYwCEuGaosr9aH","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://repo.hex.pm/preview/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.2/README.md","prompt":"List every OAuth scope name the README mentions exactly as written (e.g. ACTIVITY:READ, CALENDAR:WRITE), state whether scopes are comma- or space-separated, and quote any text about refresh tokens, token expiry, expires_in, or which scopes are required/default. Quote the relevant sentences verbatim."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":36432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":833},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36b9e331-29f4-4cd2-ab10-f29d34554d46","uuid":"6d5e2d15-1359-439a-adb0-521ae05a25cd","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:55:00.867Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzFtMtbNXtqzs3W2ydQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01U4Ewg9ydTYwCEuGaosr9aH":{"url":"https://repo.hex.pm/preview/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.2/README.md","prompt":"List every OAuth scope name the README mentions exactly as written (e.g. ACTIVITY:READ, CALENDAR:WRITE), state whether scopes are comma- or space-separated, and quote any text about refresh tokens, token expiry, expires_in, or which scopes are required/default. Quote the relevant sentences verbatim."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U4Ewg9ydTYwCEuGaosr9aH","type":"tool_result","content":"**Scope names mentioned in the README**\n\n- `ACTIVITY:READ`\n- `WELLNESS:READ`\n- `WELLNESS:WRITE`\n- `SETTINGS:READ`\n- `CALENDAR:WRITE`\n\nThe README's scope table also lists these base names, each used with a `:READ` or `:WRITE` suffix: `ACTIVITY`, `WELLNESS`, `CALENDAR`, `CHATS`, `LIBRARY`, `SETTINGS`. It also mentions `ATHLETES`, which it says doesn't work with bearer tokens.\n\n**Separator:** Scopes are comma-separated. The README says: \"intervals.icu joins scopes with **commas**, not the spaces used by most OAuth 2.0 providers\"\n\n**Refresh tokens and expiry**\n\n- \"There is no refresh token and no expiry.\" (the README bolds \"no refresh token\" and \"no expiry\")\n- \"`auth.credentials` always comes back with `refresh_token: nil`, `expires: false` and `expires_at: nil`.\"\n- \"Store the access token and use it until it stops working. There is no refresh cycle to implement.\"\n\n**expires_in:** The README doesn't mention `expires_in`.\n\n**Required and default scopes**\n\n- No scope is described as strictly required for sign-in. The README says the default is: \"The default is `\"ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ,SETTINGS:READ\"`.\"\n- The athlete endpoint needs `SETTINGS:READ`: \"**That endpoint requires `SETTINGS:READ`**\"\n- On why the default includes it: \"`SETTINGS:READ` is in there because `:fetch_athlete` defaults to `true` and `/api/v1/athlete/0` requires it.\"\n- For custom defaults: \"If you override `:default_scope`, either keep `SETTINGS:READ` or set `fetch_athlete: false`\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36b9e331-29f4-4cd2-ab10-f29d34554d46","uuid":"663329de-590a-415d-82ce-fea7ae1e300b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:55:10.098Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":10050,"code":200,"codeText":"","result":"**Scope names mentioned in the README**\n\n- `ACTIVITY:READ`\n- `WELLNESS:READ`\n- `WELLNESS:WRITE`\n- `SETTINGS:READ`\n- `CALENDAR:WRITE`\n\nThe README's scope table also lists these base names, each used with a `:READ` or `:WRITE` suffix: `ACTIVITY`, `WELLNESS`, `CALENDAR`, `CHATS`, `LIBRARY`, `SETTINGS`. It also mentions `ATHLETES`, which it says doesn't work with bearer tokens.\n\n**Separator:** Scopes are comma-separated. The README says: \"intervals.icu joins scopes with **commas**, not the spaces used by most OAuth 2.0 providers\"\n\n**Refresh tokens and expiry**\n\n- \"There is no refresh token and no expiry.\" (the README bolds \"no refresh token\" and \"no expiry\")\n- \"`auth.credentials` always comes back with `refresh_token: nil`, `expires: false` and `expires_at: nil`.\"\n- \"Store the access token and use it until it stops working. There is no refresh cycle to implement.\"\n\n**expires_in:** The README doesn't mention `expires_in`.\n\n**Required and default scopes**\n\n- No scope is described as strictly required for sign-in. The README says the default is: \"The default is `\"ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ,SETTINGS:READ\"`.\"\n- The athlete endpoint needs `SETTINGS:READ`: \"**That endpoint requires `SETTINGS:READ`**\"\n- On why the default includes it: \"`SETTINGS:READ` is in there because `:fetch_athlete` defaults to `true` and `/api/v1/athlete/0` requires it.\"\n- For custom defaults: \"If you override `:default_scope`, either keep `SETTINGS:READ` or set `fetch_athlete: false`\"","durationMs":9223,"url":"https://repo.hex.pm/preview/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.2/README.md"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U4Ewg9ydTYwCEuGaosr9aH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
