{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzNU6KZYySDB52dG2bV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the three problems in the code and wrote the causes to `ANSWER.md`. The Connect button should work now. The authorize step still depends on two things I couldn't check here: the deploy's client credentials and the calendar scopes.\n\n**What was wrong**\n\n1. **Connect always returned `unauthorized`.** The button was a plain link. The sign-in token lives in `localStorage` and only the SPA's `fetch` wrapper sends it, so the browser navigation arrived without it. Fixed: `/api/intervals/auth/init` now returns the authorize URL as JSON, and the button fetches it with the token and then navigates.\n\n2. **Pasting the authorize link returned `400 invalid_request`.** Two candidates:\n   - **Placeholder client credentials (fixed).** `config.py` says the real pair is in the deploy environment, but the code hardcoded `tricoach-dev`. It now reads `INTERVALS_CLIENT_ID` and `INTERVALS_CLIENT_SECRET`, and startup warns if the placeholder is still in use. I couldn't confirm the deploy sets these.\n   - **Calendar scopes added 2026-10-02 (not fixed).** Intervals may not allow them for this registration. A third-party README lists `CALENDAR:WRITE` but doesn't confirm `CALENDAR:READ`, and I couldn't check the official docs. Someone needs to check the scopes against the app registration in Intervals.\n\n3. **Connected for an hour, then \"reconnect\".** Rivera's token response had no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token`. The server invented a 3600-second lifetime, and the refresher then expired the connection with no way to renew it. Fixed: a missing `expires_in` means no local expiry. A connection is marked expired only when Intervals returns 401 for its token. The refresher also no longer holds the global lock during network calls.\n\n**Verification**\n- Both files compile.\n- I ran the flow locally against a mock Intervals that returns no `expires_in` or `refresh_token`. Connect, callback, status and wellness all behaved as intended.\n- The expiry paths passed in-process against the mock.\n- The real authorize step is untested. My test script briefly sent one GET with a dummy token to the real `intervals.icu` host (it returned 403) because I forgot to set `INTERVALS_BASE`. Nothing was submitted or reported.\n- I removed my scratch files from the repo and didn't commit anything.\n\n**Still needed**\n- Set the two client environment variables on deploy.\n- Confirm the scopes with Intervals, including `CALENDAR:READ`.\n- Have Rivera and the other athletes reconnect. Rivera's current connection is stale.\n- `logs/connect-attempt.log` contains a partial access token. Redact it and consider revoking Rivera's token.\n\nSources for the third-party claims: [Intervals.icu OAuth support forum thread](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759) and the [ueberauth_intervals_icu 0.1.2 README](https://repo.hex.pm/preview/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.2/README.md). The README says scopes are comma-separated and that there is no refresh token or expiry. It is a third-party library, not official docs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1870,"cache_read_input_tokens":55845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1870},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36b9e331-29f4-4cd2-ab10-f29d34554d46","uuid":"7efda469-e65a-466a-9b94-8d640eb1abe4","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:56:34.848Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzNTpxXc7LR4uxLYoFU"}
